{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01RpRycPosC4EWWMsDWfvKJ2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Curriculum â€” Decision Log Summary\n\nGrounded bullet claims drawn from the Curriculum Decision Log member document:\n\n- **The log is append-only and history-preserving.** Each entry records date, decision, who recommended it, what was selected, and why. New decisions go on top; retired ones get a strikethrough plus a \"retired YYYY-MM-DD\" line â€” history is never rewritten.\n\n- **Phase 4 quarantined decisions were resolved 2026-05-04 PM** in an interactive walkthrough that followed an autonomous overnight run. Three Phase 4 sub-decisions were settled.\n\n- **Modern-language strategic call (Phase 4 #3): Latin + Spanish selected.** Latin stays baked into the spine (e.g. Latin-3-Cicero at G9); Spanish is added as the modern-language complete track. Rationale: Spanish has the largest free OER corpus, highest practical-fluency value for an American homeschool student, and matches Hillsdale K-12 reference schools. Choosing a single modern language (not Spanish + French) keeps Phase 7b/8.4 editorial scope manageable; a third language is deferred to a Phase 9 enhancement. Downstream: Phase 8.4 (Modern Language complete track) greenlit-pending.\n\n- **American-History-Hillsdale-11 (Phase 4 #2): deferred until Phase 6 transcripts land.** Not built, not deleted â€” queued for build after Phase 6 (next 10 Hillsdale Online courses). Rationale: Phase 3 supplied 22 candidate-spine lectures (*American Heritage* Ã—12, *The Great American Story* Ã—10); building before Phase 6 means rebuilding once more sources arrive. Defer-then-build is cheaper than build-now-then-redo.\n\n- **Group A â€” modern-language stubs superseded by the Phase 8.4 Spanish track.** `middle/grade-7/Latin-6-or-Modern-Language-1/` was **reframed as Latin-track-only** (Track field + README rewritten): it already holds a fully-built Latin 6 / Henle First Year Part B course, and the \"or-Modern-Language-1\" suffix was a legacy placeholder. With Phase 8.4 installing `Spanish-2-Intermediate/` at its own G7 slot, Latin and Spanish became parallel courses rather than either-or. A folder rename is queued for a supervised cleanup pass (the sandbox cannot rename). The grade-8 entry is analogously affected.\n\n- **Phase 4 #4 first pass: four elementary stubs each kept as a real gap** â€” `grade-4/Grammar-Diagramming/` (its own discipline, complements G3 Grammar-Parts-of-Speech), `grade-4/Writing-Wise-Bauer-WWE/` (elementary precursor to the populated G5 WWS-1), `grade-5/Grammar-Complete/` (capstone consolidating G3+G4 grammar), and a fourth â€” all flagged \"build later.\"\n\n- **Group B â€” three elementary stubs later built as stub-with-spec.** `grade-4/Grammar-Diagramming/` got a ~1,300-word stub-with-spec: spine is Mary Daly's *Diagramming the Sentences of the Catechism* (Reed-Kellogg primary) with Reed & Kellogg's 1875 *Graded Lessons in English* as the public-domain alternate; 6 units / 120 lessons / 60 hours; co-runs with `K4-WRITING-WISE-BAUER-WWE`; synthesis via visual-diff machine grading on diagram correctness. `grade-4/Writing-Wise-Bauer-WWE/` is the second of the three.\n\n- **Apparent progression in the record:** the same elementary courses move from \"keep as real gap / build later\" (Phase 4 #4) to \"stub-with-spec built\" (Group B), consistent with the log's append-only, top-of-stack convention.\n\nA note on scope: this summary reflects only the anchor excerpts surfaced from the single member document (the Curriculum Decision Log). Some entries (the grade-8 Group A row, the fourth Phase 4 #4 stub, the third Group B course) are truncated in the anchors, so their dispositions are partial here."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4276,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":42685,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemer